motion of the particle as it moves along the path), then ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement.\n\n- Statement I is false, while statement II is true. It's clear from the picture below that $F$  works against the motion of the particle as it moves from $A$ to $B.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068563/assets/1764bfc51a25475162a70bad7239a36f5d099aa6157c71ed7ed3e02e474eb906.png)\n\n \n\nSo, ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0.$\n\n- Statement III is true. It's clear from the picture below that if we reverse the orientation of $C,$ then $F$ assists the motion of the particle as it moves from $B$ to $A.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068563/assets/059731f0cac61f19382172192c6a9f7f366ecb758767797f9bc8311faa3865af.png)\n\n \n\nSo, ${\\int }_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357711 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "dab6bfb9-608d-5ff8-88e7-5aa9612acda4" :knowledge-point/title "Interpreting the Sign of a Line Integral Over a Constant Vector Field"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "28d061fd-548b-54ca-b772-3c24ce1f4d9f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357713} {:answer/id #uuid "06b2bd2c-7fa4-521c-997f-ce63b44be6f2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357714} {:answer/id #uuid "8138ec7e-9a95-580d-b607-670c86d27bdd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357715} {:answer/id #uuid "482f45c5-62af-55d3-94ba-825828f367a4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357716} {:answer/id #uuid "8f72d81a-b362-5fea-bae7-05dad6148887" :an