\\text{d}r=0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357725 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3d72127a-90d6-5f7e-bd87-75d03285a918" :knowledge-point/title "Interpreting the Sign of a Line Integral Over a Non-Constant Vector Field"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2ec6f02b-55af-5961-8387-e2d9d6637e1f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357727} {:answer/id #uuid "7ca5e6df-3e3c-58e2-91c3-5bfc688aa22e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357728} {:answer/id #uuid "98d340ca-0b1b-537b-882c-0a5cd19a52c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357729} {:answer/id #uuid "bd0971a7-a127-5a2b-86de-9df5a0c95f4c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357730} {:answer/id #uuid "bdc756be-393a-5548-909a-ef64d86ebc20" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357731}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2ec6f02b-55af-5961-8387-e2d9d6637e1f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357727} :answer-field/id #uuid "a56d3748-13b7-543c-adaa-caa5aae71117" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357726}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "621ceff2-e78a-53fc-b237-4d4202c94b33" :question/math-academy-id "q-125688" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068563/assets/b9dd2fb4478ac443020e9cbebd64a2c9e4cdf5c7b6d5ce5cede854e0d7a3d804.png)\n\nConsider the vector field $F(x,y)$ shown above. Let $C$ be the path where the curve is traversed f